// Machine local overrides for the noctalia-with-niri niri session.
//
// config.kdl includes this file last, so anything written here wins over the
// shared defaults, the palette rendered by Noctalia and host.kdl. Home Manager
// creates this file only when it is missing and never rewrites it, so your
// edits survive rebuilds. Keep it out of xdg.configFile: a managed file would
// be a read-only store symlink.
//
// The `nirimod` command in this session opens this file by default, so the
// graphical window rule editor writes here instead of the read-only config.kdl.

// What merges and what does not.
//
// Merged per property, so only write the keys you want to change:
//   input, cursor, layout, debug, blur, animations, gestures, overview.
// Merged per entry, so only write the entries you want to change: binds (the
//   keys you name replace the existing bind on that key, every other bind is
//   kept; Mod+X and Super+X count as the same key), environment (appended,
//   later value wins).
// Take the last value written: screenshot-path, prefer-no-csd.
// Appended and matched in order: window-rule and layer-rule. All matching
// rules apply, so a later rule refines an earlier one. A property can only be
// given another value, never unset.
//
// Two traps worth knowing:
//   * output and workspace blocks are appended, and niri uses the FIRST block
//     matching an output, so a second block for the same output here is
//     ignored, not merged. Edit
//     hosts/<host>/desktop/noctalia-with-niri/niri-host.kdl instead.
//   * input { keyboard { xkb { ... } } }, touchpad, mouse, trackpoint and
//     trackball are replaced whole. Writing a partial touchpad block drops the
//     settings you left out.

// A syntax error here is worse than a missing file. niri keeps the running
// config when a reload fails, but a login parses this file at startup, and on
// failure niri falls back to its stock default config and drops everything
// this repo declares. Validate after editing:
//
//   niri validate -c ~/.config/niri-noctalia/config.kdl

// Remove the leading "//" from an example below to use it.

// Tighter gaps and a thicker border:
// layout {
//     gaps 8
//     border {
//         width 4
//     }
// }

// Extra key bindings, replacing the shared ones with the same key:
// binds {
//     Mod+Shift+T { spawn "alacritty"; }
// }

// Environment for processes niri spawns:
// environment {
//     MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND "1"
// }

// Keep this empty block: the graphical editor (nirimod) stores comments as
// trivia attached to a parsed node, so a file with no nodes at all loses every
// comment above on its first save. An empty layout block parses to no
// properties and therefore changes nothing. Remove it and the next save from
// the GUI collapses this file to a single line.
layout {
}
